All 3 subjects now pass structure validation. But note: 数据结构 took 3 rounds (25.9s) — meaning it needed full repair rounds. That's the pipeline working as intended (local validation now blocks). Good, and it demonstrates the loop.

However 3 rounds for every such case increases latency. Acceptable — and it's the safety net working.

Hmm, one concern: the repair loop is now triggered by point-sum mismatches which could be frequent. 数据结构 3 rounds: 18668 tokens. That's ~3x cost. Might be worth adding a cheap local auto-fix: if total points mismatch, adjust the last question's points automatically. That's a deterministic fix — cheap and reliable! "能算的不要问模型".

Yes — implement `autoHealPoints(paper, spec)`: if sum != target, distribute difference to the last question (clamp 1..50). If after adjustment valid, no repair needed.

That's a great engineering touch: deterministic repair before model repair. Let me add to paper-schema.js as part of normalizePaper, or in pipeline after normalize.

Implement in normalizePaper: after building questions, adjust:
```js
const total = questions.reduce(...)
const diff = spec.totalPoints - total
if (diff !== 0) {
  // 把差值加到最后一题（若会导致分值非法，则均摊）
  ...
}
issues.push(`分值合计 ${total}，已自动调整为 ${spec.totalPoints}`)
```
Careful: shifting points by diff could make a question negative. Clamp: if diff positive → add to last question. If negative → subtract from largest question(s).

Let me implement robustly:
```js
function reconcilePoints(questions, target) {
  if (questions.length === 0) return
  let total = questions.reduce((s,q)=>s+q.points,0)
  let diff = target - total
  if (Math.abs(diff) < 0.01) return
  // 从分值最大的题开始吸收差值，保证每题 >=1
  const order = questions.map((q,i)=>i).sort((a,b)=>questions[b].points-questions[a].points)
  for (const i of order) {
    if (Math.abs(diff) < 0.01) break
    const q = questions[i]
    const min = 1
    if (diff > 0) { q.points += diff; diff = 0 }
    else {
      const absorb = Math.min(q.points - min, -diff)
      q.points -= absorb
      diff += absorb
    }
  }
  // 剩余无法吸收则按均分处理（target 太小）
}
```
Then recompute. This makes total always match when feasible.

Then local validation should pass for points.

This is a genuinely good "验证比生成便宜" implementation: deterministic auto-heal before expensive repair.

Let me add to paper-schema.js and call it inside normalizePaper.

Also update issues message to reflect auto-adjust (informational, not blocking).

Then re-run robustness test to see rounds drop.

Let me implement.

